      "id": 1,
      "text": "Holly Ridge grew from a 1940s farming hamlet to a 1,000‑resident boom town when Camp Davis Army post opened in 1943.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holly_Ridge%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s largest employer is J&J Snack Foods, a regional leader in snack production.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holly_Ridge%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Camp Davis Industrial Park, built on former military land, now hosts Gulfstream Steel and Onslow Bay Boatworks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holly_Ridge%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Holly Ridge serves as the gateway to Topsail Island, linking inland residents to the Atlantic coast.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holly_Ridge%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s economy still feels Camp Lejeune’s pull, supporting defense contractors and services for 150,000 military families.",
